Subject: [PATCH 03971/11362] [outer-loop] known-issue: exp4729 (held-out
 first-win SCORE) deterministically exceeds codex 4800s cap

Watchdog (.435): PHASE A4 exp4729 FAILed 2x on the codex hard wall-clock cap (12:35, 13:58 UTC),
3rd attempt running. The 3-fail-skip (MAX_FAILURES_PER_TASK=3) will retire it after the 3rd fail
and advance to A5, but it burned ~4h and produced ~0 commits this window. Root cause: the
held-out-proxy readiness script runs >4800s; codex kills it every time. Operator fix: scope it
down / checkpoint-resume / route off codex. Planner: do not re-propose the full-proxy SCORE on
codex without addressing the cap.

